{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Resource","doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"externalID":"s:7Systems13SystemProfileV","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Profiling.swift#L77","fileName":"Profiling.swift"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"SystemProfile","roleHeading":"Structure"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/init()"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/timings"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Insert a profile into a world to find out where a schedule spends its time. Every schedule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that runs on the world then records each system’s runs in it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","world.resources.insert(SystemProfile())","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","","let timings = world.resources[SystemProfile.self].timings","print(timings.map(\\.name))","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\"]\"","print(timings.map(\\.runs))","\/\/ Prints \"[2, 2]\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" also holds the total, average, longest and latest time of the system’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A run’s time covers the system’s own work, measured on a continuous clock: not its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conditions, nor the commands it queued, which apply after its wave. A system its conditions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skip doesn’t run, so nothing is recorded for it. Systems in the same wave run at the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time, so their times can add up to more than the wave took. Insert a new profile to start","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile/timings":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/timings","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timings"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems12SystemTimingV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SystemTiming"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"timings","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The timing of each system that has run, in the order the systems first ran."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile\/timings"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule runs them."}],"kind":"article","title":"Scheduling Systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Resource":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Resource","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type that a world can hold a single value of, outside any entity.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Resource","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Resource","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"Resource","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/resource","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"type":"topic","title":"Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SystemTiming","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming"},"doc://Systems/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile/init()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates an empty profile."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"title":"init()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/init()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile\/init()","role":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}